Disable xmlsitemap cron regeneration in the profile's shipped config.

The osu_standard install crashes intermittently under `drush site:install`
with:

  TypeError: call_user_func_array(): Argument #1 ($callback) must be a valid
  callback, function "xmlsitemap_batch_variable_set" not found ...
  in _drush_batch_worker() (drush/includes/batch.inc:257)

Root cause: cron runs during install, and xmlsitemap_cron() calls
xmlsitemap_run_unprogressive_batch('xmlsitemap_regenerate_batch'). Under CLI
that dispatches via drush_backend_batch_process(), which processes the batch in
a Drush subprocess. xmlsitemap_regenerate_batch() defines no 'file' key, so its
operation callbacks (xmlsitemap_batch_variable_set, etc. — defined in
xmlsitemap.module) are never loaded in that subprocess and call_user_func_array
throws a TypeError. Via the web installer xmlsitemap.module is always loaded, so
the bug only surfaces under Drush.

The TypeError propagates up through module_installer->install([...]) inside the
profile's osu_standard_default_modules task and aborts it mid-way, leaving
modules such as osu_block_types (and their entity_reference_revisions /
date_ap_style / metatag field-type config) written to active storage but never
enabled. Every subsequent `drush en` then fails with
"The '<field_type>' plugin does not exist", producing an empty, unbuildable
site.

xmlsitemap_cron() short-circuits before building the batch when
disable_cron_regeneration is TRUE (see xmlsitemap.module:197-199), so shipping
the profile config with it enabled makes `drush site:install` deterministic. It
only affects cron-driven sitemap *file* regeneration (not link indexing), which
a fresh install / migration rebuild does not need; any site can re-enable it in
active config post-install.

diff --git a/config/install/xmlsitemap.settings.yml b/config/install/xmlsitemap.settings.yml
--- a/config/install/xmlsitemap.settings.yml
+++ b/config/install/xmlsitemap.settings.yml
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 lastmod_format: 'Y-m-d\TH:i\Z'
 gz: false
 clean_url: 0
-disable_cron_regeneration: false
+disable_cron_regeneration: true
 i18n_selection_mode: simple
 cron_threshold_error: 1209600
 cron_threshold_warning: 172800
